"Purpose & Standards\r\n🎯 Purpose & Standards\r\n🪖 Mission\r\nHandle every policy change as both a service request and a coverage-review opportunity. Complete the change efficiently, educate the client, protect every affected policy, and document the transaction from intake through carrier confirmation.\r\n➕ Standards of Success\r\n* Review all affected policies and renewals, follow agency coverage standards, and explain premium or coverage effects.\r\n* Enter every change request in EZLynx, complete it on the call when possible, or set a clear deadline and follow-up plan.\r\n* Verify the carrier’s official confirmation against the request before closing, then give the client the updated documents.\r\n🗂️ EZLynx & File Standards\r\n* Discussion title — Policy Change Request; use Policy Change Request Quote when quoting\r\n* Automation Center — Policy Change Request; use Policy Change Request Quote when quoting\r\n* Folder — Policy Changes/Declarations\r\n* Document labels — Certificates, Change Request Form, Signed Change Form, Endorsement; use Policy Change Request Quote when quoting\r\n* EZLynx labels — Policy Change Request; Policy Change Request Quote; Additional Policy when a coverage enhancement is completed\r\n🚫 Non-Negotiables (Unacceptable Actions)\r\n* Never omit the EZLynx change request, adequate notes, checklist documentation, signed change form, or required coverage selection form.\r\n* Never bind an agency-bill endorsement before required payment or finance confirmation is received.\r\n* Never close or confirm a request without a carrier download or a manual policy entry supported by official declarations or endorsement documents.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nStandard Operating Procedures\r\n📋 Standard Operating Procedure\r\nStep 1 — Process the Change\r\nRole: CSR / Technician\r\n* Confirm the client, policy, requested effective date, billing type, urgency, and whether the change affects other policies, an umbrella, or an offered renewal.\r\n* Use the Policy Change Intake Question Guide under Tools, Scripts & Resources: ask every Core Question, complete only the applicable Personal, Commercial, or Trucking branch, then ask every Final Verification question. Gather all required details and documents, address known claims or losses, and celebrate positive client changes.\r\n* If the client only wants a quote, label the request as a Policy Change Request Quote and do not process the endorsement until the client approves and any required payment is collected.\r\n* Enter the change on every applicable policy in EZLynx. Use a precise memo, save answers and communications to the generated task, and confirm that the Policy Change Request label is present.\r\n* For direct bill, process through the carrier portal when available or send the request to the carrier. For agency bill, obtain the endorsement invoice or quote, complete the Accounting Policy Change checklist, and collect or arrange payment before binding.\r\nRole: Producer / Account Manager\r\n* Handle licensed coverage advice, disputed effective dates, unusual underwriting questions, deficiencies found during the coverage review, or any request outside the technician’s authority.\r\nStep 2 — Reassign to CSR for follow up\r\nRole: CSR / Technician\r\n* Keep the generated task open and Reassign to CSR for follow up for carrier download or manual confirmation. Record the carrier submission date, promised turnaround time, and every contact attempt.\r\n* For routine carrier requests, follow up twice at 48-hour intervals. For a time-sensitive endorsement such as an Additional Insured or Waiver of Subrogation, call underwriting if there is no status within 48 hours.\r\n* Notify the client in writing when the carrier gives a prolonged timeline. When client information is missing, send email and text with a prominent 1–2 week deadline and document the follow-up plan.\r\nStep 3 — Confirm the Change\r\nRole: CSR / Technician\r\n* Obtain the carrier download, declarations, endorsement, ID cards, payment details, and any changed policy forms. Verify the effective date, insured items, drivers, locations, coverages, deductibles, premium, additional interests, and requested forms against the original request.\r\n* Save confirmation documents in the client file and share client-facing documents through Client Center. Update the EZLynx Details page and every affected policy or renewal.\r\n* Confirm the change request only after the system transaction and official documentation agree. Close the task with a complete note and send the client the Policy Change Processed or closeout communication.\r\nRole: Producer / Account Manager\r\n* For Commercial Lines changes with premium over $15,000, double-check the transaction before it is confirmed. Review mismatches, unsigned carrier documents, \r\n* coverage concerns, and escalations\r\n* Interest-Party Reference\r\n* • For a mortgagee, loss payee, lienholder, or leasing-company change, capture the exact legal name, address, loan or lease number, effective date, and supporting request. Confirm the carrier change and save evidence in EZLynx.\r\n* .\r\n\r\n\r\nWhat Ifs\r\n🙃 What Ifs\r\nNo change processed \r\nTell the client clearly by phone or in writing that no change has been made to the policy.\r\nNo trained processor available\r\nA technician collects the complete department question set, pastes it into the call summary, starts the EZLynx checklist, and Reassign to CSR for follow up..\r\nCarrier service center transfer\r\nUse this only when the change affects one policy. Stay on the line, record the representative’s name and completion confirmation, and still enter the EZLynx request for verification.\r\nClient lacks information/No response\r\nState in email and text that the change cannot be processed, give a 1–2 week response deadline, make two documented attempts, then close with a complete note.\r\nPremium change unknown\r\nSet expectations and contact the client as soon as the endorsement arrives so the premium explanation comes from StreetSmart.\r\nCarrier portal inaccessible\r\nAlert the Team Lead and use the approved carrier submission alternative.\r\nPayment missing or fails\r\nDo not bind the agency-bill change. Alert the Team Lead and resolve payment or financing first.\r\nCarrier documentation unsigned\r\nAlert the Account Manager and obtain the required signatures before confirmation.\r\nNo proof change was bound\r\nKeep the request open and alert the Account Manager; do not confirm until official carrier evidence is received.\r\nPolicy/Endorsement discrepancy\r\nDo not confirm it. Alert the Team Lead or Account Manager and correct the dates, coverage, or insured items with the carrier.\r\nCarrier site error\r\nCollect all endorsement information, tell the insured a callback is required, and avoid leaving the client on hold.\r\nQuote only request\r\nUse the Policy Change Request Quote workflow and do not process or bind until the client approves.\r\nNo download/Client needs proof\r\nObtain an ID card or other proof directly from the carrier; temporary proof may be issued only when authorized by your team lead, and the request remains open until manual transaction and declarations are saved.\r\nFuture-dated request\r\nProcess it on the correct effective date, verify the declarations, and check that a current-term display does not cause the change to be applied early.\r\nRequest to carrier lacks detail\r\nAlways include the effective date and complete coverage or quote-change details in the email and attached request.\r\nMissing download fields\r\nObtain an official declarations page, amended endorsement, or carrier-portal summary. Upload it, verify the request, and only then confirm the change. Verify addresses with USPS and Google Maps and ask the carrier to correct mapping errors.\r\nSeparate vehicle/driver changes\r\nThey may be separated when necessary, but document each transaction and aim to complete both the same day; identify carrier-specific underwriting delays.\r\nCarrier binds quote-only request\r\nSave all correspondence and representative name, instruct carrier not to process, and alert Team Lead immediately.\r\nUnresponsive carrier\r\nFor urgent requests, call underwriting after 48 hours. For routine requests, make two follow-ups 48 hours apart and document each with system labels; escalate after the second attempt. Tell the client promptly about long carrier timelines.\r\nWrong contact information\r\nUse the Postal Mail process and send the Bad Contact memo.\r\nPost-submission non-response\r\nComplete one coordinated call, email, and text follow-up with a deadline; notify the carrier, close with documentation, and use Postal Mail when the severity warrants it.\r\nExpired policy\r\nDo not endorse an expired contract. Close the task with “Policy expired; moving to Re-write,” then use the New Business workflow. Mercury or Plymouth Rock may require a Statement of No Loss.\r\nStale request on active policy\r\nDelete the unprocessed request in EZLynx and notify the client that no change was processed.\r\nCarrier does not issue endorsement\r\nConfirm the change in the system with what we requested only after we confirm it was received and processed\r\nHelpful Resources and Links\r\n📁 Tools, Scripts & Resources\r\nEmail and voice templates\r\n* Search EZLynx email templates for POLICY CHANGE REQUEST. Use the appropriate Quote, Carrier Request, Follow-Up, Pending, Processed, Closeout, or Not Processed template; keep the change PDF attached when following up.\r\n* Use the carrier voicemail template to request confirmation and include the policy number and request date. Use the congratulatory, coverage-decrease, coverage-increase, and cross-sell scripts when appropriate.\r\nPolicy Change Intake Question Guide\r\nUse this guide to process changes by category. Ask the Core Questions first, then address the functional category needed, applying specific line nuances as required.\r\nCore Questions (Required for Every Change)\r\n* Who is requesting the change, and have you verified the client, account, and authority?\r\n* What exactly needs to change, why, and which policy or policies are affected?\r\n* What effective date is requested, and are there any known claims or losses?\r\n* Could this affect other policies, renewals, umbrella, or additional interests?\r\n* What supporting details/documents are required, and what expectations must be explained?\r\nAddress Change\r\n* Universal: Are the mailing address, garaging address, and residence changing? Does this apply to other policies?\r\n* Personal Nuances: If mailing-only, why? List all household members (Name, DOB, DL). Own or rent? Registration matches policy state? Explain territory rate impact.\r\n* Commercial/Trucking Nuances: Is the business location changing? Does this affect federal/state filings or registrations?\r\nAdd Driver / Employee\r\n* Universal: Full name, DOB, DL/CDL number, licensing state, verified residential address, and relationship to insured.\r\n* Personal Nuances: Occupation/education status? Good-student discount (GPA 3.0+) or away-from-home (100+ miles) eligible? Driver training completed?\r\n* Commercial/Trucking Nuances: Job duties, CDL issue year, and MVR history. Will they take vehicles home? Obtain signed exclusion if unacceptable.\r\nRemove Driver / Employee\r\n* Universal: Reason for removal (Sold, traded, totaled, no longer employed/living there).\r\n* Nuances: If still in household/employed, obtain proof of other insurance or signed exclusion. Divorce: Obtain signature/decree. Trucking: Obtain lease-termination for filings.\r\nAdd Vehicle / Trailer / Inland Marine\r\n* Universal: VIN, year, make, model, purchase date, value, garaging location, lienholder details, and desired deductibles.\r\n* Personal Nuances: Turo/Uber/Rideshare use? Rental/Towing/Glass/GAP needed?\r\n* Commercial/Trucking Nuances: Registration/Title obtained? Operating radius? Modifications (wraps, shelving)? Equipment details (SN/Weight/Length) and 4-side photos.\r\nRemove Vehicle / Trailer / Inland Marine\r\n* Universal: Unit being removed and why. Still in client's possession? Proof provided (Bill of Sale/Plate Surrender)?\r\nCoverage / Operation Changes\r\n* Universal: Liability limits or deductibles requested? Obtain signed coverage-selection forms.\r\n* Personal Nuances: Scheduled Jewelry (Brand/Size/Appraisal/Safe)? Travel details (domestic/international) and wearing frequency?\r\n* Commercial/Trucking Nuances: Class code/Operation change? Alternate Employer details? Filing/Authority removal reason?\r\nLegal / Entity / Interest Changes\r\n* Universal: Misspelling, marriage, divorce, or legal name change? Is ownership/insurable interest changing?\r\n* Nuances: Divorce: Obtain decree and proof of new address. Trust/LLC: Obtain formation docs and identify principals. POA: Verify authority document. Deceased: Obtain death certificate and executor docs.\r\nFinal Verification — Ask for Every Policy Change\r\n* Have you confirmed every affected policy, vehicle, driver, property, location, operation, coverage, and additional interest?\r\n* Have you restated the requested change and effective date and confirmed that all required answers and documents are complete?\r\n* Does the client understand that the change is not complete until carrier approval or official confirmation is received?\r\n* How and when will the client receive the status update and final documents?\r\nTrackers and working links\r\n* Open Policy Change Tracker: https://drive.google.com/open?id=1-_Egm_2K16aAQv8u_MqKzWJGFTEr4KA8reh_oFm3rg4\r\n* Policy Change Request live page and full department question banks: https://sites.google.com/streetsmart.insurance/siteswiki/sops-standard-operating-procedures/policy-change-request\r\n* Coverage Standards training video: https://www.loom.com/share/31bf6f81d999433f8e4040349858e066\r\n* Future-dated change video: https://www.loom.com/share/de6521eb0b884b81ba66058b7336e780\r\n* EZLynx policy change request instructions: https://ezlynxsupport.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/8000064135-policies-creating-managing-your-policies#Endorsements,-Policy-Changes,-&-Policy-Change-Requests\r\n* Client Center payment request: https://ezlynxsupport.freshdesk.com/support/solutions/articles/8000094646-client-center-payment-request\r\n* Truck Carrier List: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1EUitDqDjgPWh9vcTu7mQAcm62up9JooqGDqZDkWvh3U/edit\r\n* VIN confirmation guide: https://docs.google.com/document/d/1NttFZMeriK7HA-ecawYSSWIFg5aIiObfzaDWoF10q1o/edit\r\nTraining Assets\r\nInfographic: Policy Change Request Workflow SOP\r\nAudio Overview: The Policy Change Request SOP\r\nVideo Overview: How to Execute the Policy Change Request SOP\r\nQuiz: Policy Quiz\r\nROBIE Reference Fields\r\nPurpose\r\nStandardize how policy change requests are received, documented in EZLynx, submitted to the carrier, verified, and closed.\r\nApplies To\r\nPersonal and commercial policy changes, endorsements, additions, removals, corrections, coverage changes, and carrier follow-up.\r\nSystems Used\r\nEZLynx, carrier portals, email, phone, text messaging, Client Center, and document tools.\r\nRelated Items\r\n* EZLynx policy change request and recordkeeping standards\r\n* Document naming, upload, activity-note, and file-maintenance standards\r\n* Proof of Insurance Request SOP when temporary evidence is needed\r\n* Billing and Payments SOP when premium changes create payment action\r\n* Carrier-specific policy change skills and walkthrough videos"